## The CLI: `playwright-screenshot`

From the project or task-worktree root, every capture in this skill is a single
invocation of:

```bash
node .agents/skills/ui-visual-capture/scripts/playwright-screenshot.mjs <url> [output-path] [flags]
```

The script auto-detects the project root (walking up looking for `.git`),
finds `playwright` in your project's `node_modules` (including monorepo
subdirs like `frontend/node_modules/playwright`), captures all five viewports
in parallel, and prints a JSON summary on stdout.

Run it once with `--help` for the full reference. The most-used flags:

| Flag                                     | Effect                                                 |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| `--theme=light\|dark\|system`            | Force color scheme (default `system`)                  |
| `--viewport-only`                        | Visible region only (default: full page)               |
| `--scroll-to=SELECTOR`                   | Scroll element into view before capture                |
| `--scroll-y=N`                           | Scroll N pixels before capture                         |
| `--clip-to=SELECTOR`                     | Crop to one component: shoot only that element's bounding box |
| `--script PATH`                          | Run an interaction script then capture (enables video) |
| `--no-video`                             | Disable video even when `--script` is set              |
| `--wait-until=load\|domcontentloaded\|networkidle` | Navigation readiness; use `domcontentloaded` for Storybook iframes |
| `--storage-state PATH`                   | Use saved Playwright auth state                        |
| `--auth-token TOKEN`                     | Send `Authorization: Bearer TOKEN`                     |
| `--header K=V` (repeatable)              | Extra HTTP header                                      |
| `--resolution=low\|medium\|high\|native` | low/medium = JPEG, smaller; default `native` = PNG @2x |
| `--viewports=mobile,desktop`             | Subset, width override `mobile=375`, or exact size `mobile=390x40` |
| `--video-fps=N`                          | WebM frame extraction FPS; animation review minimum is `60` |
| `--contact-sheet-columns=N`              | Override contact sheet column count                    |
| `--contact-sheet-thumb-width=N`          | Override contact sheet thumbnail width                 |
| `--attach-existing`                      | Reuse a dev server started from a different worktree   |

Default output location must come from the **`agent-fs`** skill:

- Issue-scoped captures:
  `CAPTURES="$("$AGENT_FS_BIN" scratch "ui-visual-capture-$ISSUE")"`
- Anonymous captures:
  `CAPTURES="$("$AGENT_FS_BIN" scratch visual-capture)"`

Screenshots always default to session scratch. With a local-only tracker, do not
upload them and do not treat a missing attachment as a close blocker. Record the
exact scratch path in the structured issue comment. An attachment-capable
workflow may explicitly promote selected artifacts for upload,
but publication is separate from the default capture path.

Never write captures or helper scripts to ad hoc temp paths. On Claude Code with
`agent-fs init --runtime claude-code`, the PreToolUse hook blocks unsanctioned
temporary writes; other runtimes follow the same project rule by policy.

This is always outside the project root.

At the end, you MUST output a full folder path to the foder which contains your
captures in your agent scratch folder.

Example:

```bash
Visual captures can be viewed here: `/Users/twhoffmann/.agent-scratch/sess-59fe522d-6de1-48bd-b197-8658e8c91815/scratch/ui-visual-capture-TIZA-1006-journey-review`
```

IMPORTANT: The path must be EXACT. DO NOT ellipsise any part of it or use line breaks.

