## Sheet/modal geometry assertions

Any test or visual review that exercises a sheet, modal, drawer, or other
fixed-position overlay must include a geometry assertion against `mobile_safari`
(390 × 664). Visual screenshots alone are insufficient — they can be cropped,
scaled, or interpreted as "looks fine" when the layout is actually clipped.

### Why this exists

Before 2026-05-16, the default `mobile` viewport (390 × 844) hid a class of
real iPhone Safari regressions: modal close buttons clipped under the browser
header, sticky footers fighting the toolbar, sheets that resolve at the bottom
of `100vh` but not `100svh`. The recipe modal (`RecipeDrawer`, GRO-934) was
the canary that triggered this rule. The `mobile_safari` viewport surfaces
the bug class; the assertion below proves it is fixed.

### The assertion

```js
// At a viewport with browser chrome active (mobile_safari = 390 × 664):
const sheetBox = await page.locator('[role="dialog"]').boundingBox()
expect(sheetBox).not.toBeNull()
// Top of sheet is at least 8px below the viewport top edge (room for header
// chrome, drag handle, etc. — never flush against the chrome).
expect(sheetBox.y).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(8)
// Sheet never overflows the viewport vertically.
expect(sheetBox.height).toBeLessThanOrEqual(await page.evaluate(() => window.innerHeight))
// Bottom of sheet aligns with the bottom of the viewport, within 2px tolerance
// for sub-pixel rounding. If the sheet stops short of the bottom, the app
// bottom-nav is leaking through.
expect(
  Math.abs(sheetBox.y + sheetBox.height - (await page.evaluate(() => window.innerHeight)))
).toBeLessThanOrEqual(2)
```

Selector note: if the overlay does not yet expose `[role="dialog"]`, fix that
first — `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"` are required for screen-reader
correctness and are the canonical hook for this assertion.

### What the assertion does NOT cover

- Drag-to-dismiss gesture geometry (covered by interaction tests).
- Background scroll lock (verify separately with `page.evaluate(() => document.body.scrollTop)`).
- Focus trap behaviour (verify with `page.keyboard.press('Tab')` and accessibility tree assertions).
- Reduced-motion respect (verify with `page.emulateMedia({ reducedMotion: 'reduce' })`).

These belong in a separate test alongside the geometry assertion, not as
replacements for it.

### Where to put it

- Inside the component's own Playwright test (preferred — runs on every CI).
- Inside the interaction script passed to `playwright-screenshot --script`
  when capturing visual evidence (acts as a guard against accepting a
  visibly-broken capture).

