## Step 6 — Report; publish only when explicitly required

Always post the structured visual-review comment with the exact absolute scratch
path.

**Local-only tracker adapters:** stop there. Screenshots remain in session scratch. Do not call
`agent-fs evidence upload` or `agent-fs evidence post`, and do not block
`in_review` or issue closure because no attachment exists.

**Attachment-capable tracker adapters:** only when the workflow or
user explicitly requires publication, promote selected supported files from
scratch into a deliberate issue evidence bundle, then upload that bundle:

```bash
PUBLISH="$("$AGENT_FS_BIN" evidence --issue "$ISSUE" visual-capture-after)"
cp "$CAPTURES/after/mobile.png" "$PUBLISH/mobile.png"
cp "$CAPTURES/after/desktop.png" "$PUBLISH/desktop.png"
agent-fs evidence manifest --issue "$ISSUE" visual-capture-after
agent-fs evidence upload --issue "$ISSUE" visual-capture-after

# Or upload and post the explicit bundle in one call.
agent-fs evidence post --issue "$ISSUE" visual-capture-after \
  --comment "Visual proof — after, all viewports."
```

`evidence post` embeds attachment markdown. This publication branch is not part
of a local-only tracker workflow.

### Allowed publication file types

| Type | MIME              | Notes                                                      |
| ---- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| PNG  | `image/png`       | ✅ Screenshots and contact sheets                          |
| JPEG | `image/jpeg`      | ✅ Compressed screenshots                                  |
| GIF  | `image/gif`       | ✅ Allowed but not used for animation evidence             |
| PDF  | `application/pdf` | ✅ Reports                                                 |
| WebM | `video/webm`      | ❌ Not accepted — retain locally, upload contact sheet PNG |
| MP4  | `video/mp4`       | ❌ Not accepted                                            |

