## Acceptance criteria checklist for UI tickets

Before marking any UI ticket `in_review`, confirm:

- [ ] **Design-guide skill loaded** and the work reviewed through its lens (see "MANDATORY pre-capture gate")
- [ ] **Wireframe located and compared** against the captures — or its absence explicitly flagged to the user
- [ ] **Before screenshots** captured and reviewed (minimum: mobile + desktop)
- [ ] **After screenshots** captured and reviewed for all five viewports (incl. `mobile_safari`)
- [ ] **`mobile_safari` (390 × 664) capture** reviewed for any change that introduces or modifies a fixed/sticky/overlay layer (modal, sheet, drawer, nav, toast, banner)
- [ ] **Geometry assertion** included in the component test for any sheet/modal/drawer (see "Sheet/modal geometry assertions" section)
- [ ] **Interaction recording** captured as WebM for animation or multi-step flows
- [ ] Animation review captured with at least `--video-fps=60`; journey review uses sampling appropriate to state/outcome proof
- [ ] WebM retained locally inside the capture output directory
- [ ] WebM frames extracted inside `frames/<viewport>-webm/`
- [ ] WebM contact sheet generated inside `contact-sheets/` (60fps extraction for animation review)
- [ ] Capture manifest generated inside `manifests/`
- [ ] Contact sheet reaches the intended final UI state
- [ ] Final WebM frame verified against the settled-state PNG
- [ ] No spinner-only or blank loading-state evidence unless the ticket is specifically about loading
- [ ] All screenshots and derivative captures remain under the `agent-fs` session scratch directory
- [ ] **Structured visual review comment** posted on the issue
- [ ] Exact absolute scratch path included in the structured review comment
- [ ] For local-only trackers, no screenshot upload or attachment used as an `in_review` or close gate
- [ ] For attachment-capable adapters, any publication was explicitly required and used a deliberate evidence bundle
- [ ] Target statement recorded as `route + viewport rule + expected behavior`
- [ ] Evidence captured from one dedicated server instance (single base URL/port)
- [ ] Keyboard-only flow verified: logical focus order, visible focus indicators, no keyboard traps
- [ ] Reduced-motion behaviour verified for motion-heavy UI (`prefers-reduced-motion` respected)
- [ ] Touch targets ≥ 44px on mobile viewports
- [ ] No visible layout overflow or truncation at any breakpoint
- [ ] Colour contrast passes WCAG AA (4.5:1 text, 3:1 UI components)
- [ ] All visible date/time values in screenshots validated against `timezone_reference.py`
- [ ] Day-label/date pairing validated (for example, `Sun, 10 May 2026` => Sunday)
- [ ] Displayed time/zone validated against UTC reference and offset math

